## What I built

A fourth exclusion bucket in scripts/measure_abstentions.py — EXCLUDED_PROVIDER_ERROR.

The defect: my instrument counted produced 0 tasks as an abstention regardless of cause. Both post-#808 sessions that scored as "gradeable" ended their planner turn on error: Rate limited, retry after Some(14454000)ms — a ~4h retry-after. The turn wasn't silent after a tool; it was refused by the provider, and 0 firings there is correct behaviour (piped_should_continue requires !had_error). So every rate-limit event was manufacturing a gradeable session showing firings=0, which reads as evidence against #808 when it's evidence about Anthropic's rate limiter.

The shape, matching what this file already does:
• `classify_provider_error_line / classify_provider_error — pure, anchored exactly as classify_line is (first word → end-of-line, numbers loose, runner tab prefix allowed), every candidate through is_quoted_prose`. That filter is load-bearing here, not polish: #810's own thread carries `Rate limited` inside a markdown table — and note the direction of damage is the sharp one, since a false positive shrinks my own denominator. A shape-match that trips it is counted in prose_excluded, never dropped.
• The bucket leaves numerator and denominator both, reported on its own, never summed into INELIGIBLE / UNKNOWN_AGE / the zero-abstention exclusions.
• `MIN_GRADEABLE_SESSIONS = 4` unchanged.

I named the coarseness rather than dressing it up. @yuanhao asked for "a provider error in the same phase as the zero-task outcome." There's no cheap phase anchor in a session directory's concatenated lines, so this is session-level presence — a judgment threshold whose only evidence is that healthy sessions had zero such lines. That sentence is in the code comment and in the printed verdict. I didn't claim attribution the code doesn't perform.

Tests extended in run_self_tests(): detector both directions, three prose tells, disjointness from the abstention markers, and the near-miss guard — an abstention with no provider error grades exactly as before (Day 124: a discriminator tested only where it blocks is vacuous green). Byte-identity verified by running both tools side by side. classify_line, classify, is_quoted_prose untouched.

